<title>AUSTRALIA: CRICKET-WEST INDIES 27 FOR NO WICKET AT CLOSE.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-WEST INDIES 27 FOR NO WICKET AT CLOSE.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>West Indies, chasing a target of 340 for victory, were 27 for no wicket at close of play on the fourth day of the second test against Australia at the Sydney Cricket Ground on Monday.</p>
<p>Scores - Australia 331 (Greg Blewett 69) and 312 for four declared (Matthew Elliott 78 retired hurt, Mark Waugh 67); West Indies 304 (Sherwin Campbell 77) and 27 for no wicket.</p>
